  "slug": "design-glue-eb6f",
  "summary": "Rational design of molecular glues, antibody conjugates and binders now targets transient interfaces with improved selectivity control.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is deliberate engineering of protein-protein interfaces to control target fate or activity. Two molecular glue degrader preprints illustrate this: TrIP-MGRD targets transient PPI pockets, supported by a CDK12-DDB1 cryo-EM structure and the glue C432, while an antibody-drug conjugate of a CCNK glue degrader gives HER2-selective cyclin K degradation in breast cancer. A degron-informed study identifies DCAF10 as a targeted protein degradation E3 ligase, with an optimized Pr-GFI recruiter degrading FKBP12 and BRD9. Computational design extends the theme to PDZ-binding peptides in a shared latent space, MobGen monobodies against SARS-CoV-2 Spike RBD, and a quantum-mechanics-guided covalent recruiter of FBXO22 for BRD4 degradation. Paired deep mutational scanning of Lck yields a nilotinib-sensitized variant. The new element is rational, selective, interface-aware design, though modalities and maturity differ across items.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
